Package: jobR
Type: Package
Title: Distribute Embarrassingly Parallel Work Across Machines You Already Have
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Jared", "Norman", email = "jarednorman@hotmail.com",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Runs a batch of independent jobs across whatever machines are to
    hand -- a few laptops on a LAN, or colleagues in other countries -- with no
    cloud account, no scheduler and no paid service. A host holds the jobs and
    an append-only ledger; workers join with a spoken passphrase, fetch the
    project bundle only when it has changed, and pull chunks until the work is
    done. Chunks are leased rather than merely sent, so a worker that loses
    power or closes its lid has its work reissued automatically, and both host
    and workers can restart without losing progress.
